e{ln}⁡(1-\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta {\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-\\theta ){\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}(1-{x}_{i}) \\\\  & =S\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta +(n-S)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-\\theta )\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $S={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ is the number of successes in the sample.\n\nFinally, since there are $2$ successes in the sample, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}l(\\theta ) & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta +(8-2)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-\\theta ) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta +6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443713 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192685 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ea184595-346e-5c0c-bb95-8779d73f6f6b" :knowledge-point/title "Log-Likelihood Functions for Bernoulli Random Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ec71840-3b63-5e08-83f4-28715450f86f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta +3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-\\theta )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443624} {:answer/id #uuid "28bbbbae-0703-537d-bd9f-e05b52fb2181" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta +4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-\\theta )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443635} {:answer/id #uuid "a9e80966-cc23-561a-973b-d44c3ce7fdd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta +3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-\\theta )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443674} {:answer/id #uuid "ab107af7-aaf1-5009-9d41-de7830103788" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta +7\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-\\theta )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443675} {:answer/id #uuid "af6ffbd3-2b40-5b17-b106-49656d990b48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡