\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({\\theta }^{{x}_{i}})+\\operatorname{ln}⁡((1-\\theta )^{1-{x}_{i}}) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta +(1-{x}_{i})\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta {\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-\\theta ){\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}(1-{x}_{i}) \\\\  & =S\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta +(n-S)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-\\theta )\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $S={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ is the number of successes in the sample.\n\nFinally, since there are $3$ successes in the sample, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}l(\\theta ) & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta +(7-3)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-\\theta ) \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta +4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443716 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192685 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ea184595-346e-5c0c-bb95-8779d73f6f6b" :knowledge-point/title "Log-Likelihood Functions for Bernoulli Random Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11ae0523-db72-5ee3-ad6e-2aa05d8a483d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta +2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-\\theta )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443626} {:answer/id #uuid "15d7d119-3fa5-5cf9-8f20-28c31be19c4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta +3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-\\theta )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443627} {:answer/id #uuid "4e1b395c-5798-5603-a67e-3c9748205c63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta +5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-\\theta )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443646} {:answer/id #uuid "9feb2eab-afdd-53e9-9b35-5ea893474079" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta +5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-\\theta )"